cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Extremal Selection as an Operational Substitute for Coexponentials: Fisher-Controlled Factorization"
message: "If you use this software or its formal results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Koch"
    given-names: "Brisen"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bbis-ops/Hypersurface-Categorical-Polytope"
url: "https://github.com/bbis-ops/Hypersurface-Categorical-Polytope"
abstract: >-
  Software and formal results for Newton-tropical face selection at simple
  polyhedral vertices. The central law turns local geometry, weighted
  polynomial order, and active constraints into a finite prediction of the
  winning face and the response exponent, converting a weighted degree q into
  a gap exponent by q -> 1/(1-q). The series covers exact vertex localization
  on a bounded box (V.1-V.14), where the interaction-strength threshold is
  exactly zero and displacement, objective-gap, directional, and saturation
  laws are given in closed form; the orthant Newton-tropical law (V.15);
  qualified face selection with tangent-cone localization and non-circular
  admissibility (V.16); an exact ambient-to-face compiler that transports
  polynomials in rational arithmetic with auditable cancellation and lineage
  (V.20); a universality phase fan whose exact affine walls locate every
  change of winning mechanism over a parameter domain (V.17), together with
  the discovery engine that partitions finite perturbation families into
  exponent and mechanism classes (V.21); and certified quadratic elimination
  of curved channels,
  resolving signed perturbations that first-layer coordinate-face selection
  cannot decide (V.22). All structural computation is exact rational
  arithmetic. Model-proposed candidates are treated as untrusted data,
  screened under a syntax-tree whitelist and adjudicated locally, so results
  do not depend on which model produced them; the backend fails closed,
  declining to license a theorem whose hypotheses are unverified. The
  categorical work on coexponentials and Fisher-controlled factorization is
  the historical origin of the project.
keywords:
  - Newton polytope
  - tropical geometry
  - singular asymptotics
  - face selection
  - polyhedral geometry
  - asymptotic expansion
  - exact rational arithmetic
  - vertex localization
  - Fisher information
  - coexponential
  - category theory
  - optimization
